B19 - Find and fix a vulnerability from a GitHub project

Objective
The goal of this activity is to identify and fix a potential security vulnerability in a GitHub project.

Method
I reviewed a GitHub project to identify insecure practices and implemented improvements to reduce security risks.

Findings
- Identified insecure exposure of sensitive information within configuration examples and project files.
- Improved handling of sensitive data by recommending environment variables (.env) instead of hardcoded credentials.
- Reviewed repository structure and improved awareness of secure coding practices.

Security Principle
This activity reinforced:
- Confidentiality of sensitive information
- Vulnerability identification and mitigation
- Secure coding practices
- Risk reduction in software development

Evidence
- Screenshot of the GitHub project before improvements
- Screenshot of updated configuration/documentation after changes
- Screenshot of files showing improved credential handling practices
- Notes explaining the identified vulnerability and implemented fix

Reflection
This activity demonstrated how small vulnerabilities in repositories can create significant security risks if left unresolved. Fixing these issues improved my understanding of secure configuration management and safe development practices.
